WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Speaker 1: Let's go to Omar from Atlanta. Omar&nbsp;
from Atlanta, welcome to the program. What is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.920
on your mind today?
Speaker 2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.720
Hello? Can you hear me?
Speaker 1: Yes, I can.&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.880
Speaker 2: Yes. So I think the other Atlanta&nbsp;
gentleman had a similar question. It's kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:22.140
of about the Trump indictment recently on these&nbsp;
documents. So my question is, is that especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.840
since the Espionage Act has been used to prosecute&nbsp;
people, at least the left would assume to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.340
heroes like reality winner and whatnot. First&nbsp;
of all, what are your thoughts on the hypocrisy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:38.400
of reality? Winner from the moment of arrest to&nbsp;
being released, never saw foot outside of jail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.200
and the hypocrisy there with Trump. And secondly,&nbsp;
on whether or not we should be cheering on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:50.100
Espionage Act to be used against Trump like this.
Speaker 1: I don't have any. Philosophical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:59.100
opposition to it being used. I. It&nbsp;
is not unique that statutes and law.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.960
Can be used in ways we don't agree with. That is&nbsp;
that's not that's not a unique thing. And that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.800
alone doesn't make me say this is suspect, this is&nbsp;
bad, or whatever the case may be. We are we just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.720
got the indictment. We are eventually going to see&nbsp;
what this case is built on and we're all going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:24.540
be able to sort of judge for ourselves whether&nbsp;
the espionage is correct or incorrect. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:30.960
I think it's important to say Trump is not&nbsp;
accused of spying for another country. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.880
lot of people are hearing the word espionage&nbsp;
or Espionage Act and assuming certain things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.900
that are not actually part of the indictment,&nbsp;
let's not allow the word. I mean, the Espionage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:45.960
Act contains a number of different provisions. If&nbsp;
the indictment is accurate, Trump did violate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.000
Espionage Act doesn't mean he spied for Russia.&nbsp;
So I think it's way too certainly too early to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.980
say it's incorrect to charge him in that way.
Speaker 2: Right. Yeah, He he's charged with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.220
