them. Yeah, I guess from my perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:04.320
it's because we have that Georgia case building&nbsp;
up right now. I would much prefer to see that in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.480
the limelight than Espionage Act violations,&nbsp;
which just seems at least personally less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.060
tenuous from a political perspective.
Speaker 1: There's also a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.440
different charges, and it's obstruction and&nbsp;
it's a whole bunch of different things. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.420
it's also a false notion to say the only thing&nbsp;
Trump did wrong was having the documents. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.020
actually goes much further than that. And in&nbsp;
fact, this is the point why you have to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.820
at what Hillary was was investigated for. To&nbsp;
understand it's not about holding documents.&nbsp;

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.240
Speaker 2: And refusing to return them.&nbsp;
Yeah, absolutely. Yeah, that's fair.&nbsp;

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.940
Speaker 1: All right. Omar from&nbsp;
Atlanta, thank you for the call.&nbsp;

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.580
